# central/.dev.vars.example — local development secrets for the central Worker.
#
# `wrangler dev` auto-loads a file named `.dev.vars` from this directory into
# `env`. Get started with:
#
#   cp central/.dev.vars.example central/.dev.vars
#
# Add a key only when you need that feature locally. Non-secret config
# (BILL_PROVIDER, EMAIL_PROVIDER, …) lives in wrangler.toml — see
# central/wrangler.example.toml. Production secrets are set with
# `wrangler secret put` (see the "Secrets" note in central/wrangler.example.toml).
#
# `.dev.vars` is gitignored; this `.dev.vars.example` is committed. Never put a
# real value in this example file.

# --- Bill data provider -----------------------------------------------------
# Central fetches bills from one provider, chosen by BILL_PROVIDER in
# wrangler.toml (default "legiscan"). Set the key for whichever you use; the
# other can stay unset. Needed only when you actually ingest bills locally.
# LEGISCAN_API_KEY=         # https://legiscan.com/legiscan  — primary, maintained path
# OPENSTATES_API_KEY=       # https://open.pluralpolicy.com/accounts/profile/  — alternative, not actively maintained

# --- Admin / operator endpoints (optional) ----------------------------------
# Bearer secret protecting /admin/* and /tenants/* routes. Set it to call those
# routes locally (pass it as the x-admin-secret header); unset leaves them
# closed. Any non-empty string works for local dev.
# ADMIN_SECRET=

# --- Analytics & delivery status (optional) ---------------------------------
# Cloudflare API token (Account Analytics: Read + Zone Analytics: Read) for the
# D1 anomaly watch and email-delivery lookups. Unset disables those features.
# CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=
